# Agents

These **Agents** pages and the site `/llms.txt` are the setup path for
visiting agents and for people wiring agents into a repo. Read `/llms.txt`
first. Do not scrape the human [Docs](/docs/) lane for that sequence.

OKMate has no MCP server and no hosted query API.

:card-grid.begin
    :link-card[page: "agents/install", title: "Install", summary: "Get the okmate CLI, then confirm check works on one root."]
    :link-card[page: "agents/skills", title: "Skills", summary: "manage-okmate-knowledge lives in the repository; include it, do not fork it."]
    :link-card[page: "agents/cli", title: "CLI", summary: "JSON-oriented check, inspect, search, roots, and sync."]
:card-grid.end

## Fetch sequence

:steps.begin
    :step.begin[title: "Read this site's /llms.txt"]
        Fetch `/llms.txt` on this site. It is the product-site index (page
        titles and descriptions). It is not a bundle `okmate build` artifact.
    :step.end
    :step.begin[title: "Install okmate"]
        Follow [Install](/docs/install/). You need the `okmate` binary on
        `PATH`, or `cargo run --no-default-features -p okmate --` from a clone.
    :step.end
    :step.begin[title: "Install or point at the skill"]
        Use [`.agents/skills/manage-okmate-knowledge/SKILL.md`](/agents/skills/)
        in this repository. Point the agent at that file; do not maintain a
        drifting copy.
    :step.end
    :step.begin[title: "List roots"]
        Run `okmate roots --format paths`.
    :step.end
    :step.begin[title: "Work one root"]
        Run `check`, `inspect`, or `search` on a single path from that list.
        Commands stay single-root.
    :step.end
    :step.begin[title: "Author Markdown, then re-check"]
        Edit inert OKF Markdown in that root. Run
        `okmate check <root> --profile strict --format terminal` again.
    :step.end
:steps.end
